---
/* Rich body for the "Understanding webinar organizers" case study.
   The shared [slug].astro template renders this when the slug
   matches; the default templated layout is bypassed.
   Shared .rwc-* layout/typography lives in global.css; image
   lightbox in CaseBodyLightbox.astro. */
import CaseBodyLightbox from './CaseBodyLightbox.astro';
---

<div class="rwc-body">

  {/* ───────────────────── HERO / CONTEXT ───────────────────── */}
  <section class="rwc-hero" id="case-context">
    <div class="rwc-hero-left">
      <div class="case-cat">Case study · On-Air webinars discovery</div>
      <h1 class="case-title">Understanding webinar organizers</h1>
      <p class="case-subtitle">
        As the lead designer for On-Air webinars, I planned, prepared, and
        co-led a research study aimed at informing the future of our product.
      </p>

      <div class="rwc-callout">
        <div class="rwc-callout-title">
          <span class="rwc-callout-star" aria-hidden="true">★</span>
          Core achievements
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Ran the company's first major study to understand webinar
            organizers, building a foundational knowledge resource for the
            business unit.
          </li>
          <li>
            Generated critical insights to inform the product's roadmap, and
            briefed 2 other pods in the process.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="rwc-hero-right">
      <div class="case-img-ph rwc-hero-img is-filled" data-ratio="4-3">
        <img src="/assets/images/cases/sy-research/hero.webp" alt="StreamYard webinar registration UI — welcome to the webinar" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" />
      </div>
      <p class="case-img-caption">Image by StreamYard via streamyard.com</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ───────────────────── MY ROLE + KEY INITIATIVES ───────────────────── */}
  <section class="rwc-role" id="case-role">
    <div class="rwc-role-left">
      <div class="eyebrow">My role</div>
      <h2 class="rwc-h2">Staff Product Designer / Research co-lead</h2>

      <p>
        Assisted by our research lead, and some of our team's designers
        (as notetakers during interviews), we started by setting up a plan
        for the study and aligning with our team's project manager and
        engineering manager. Once we agreed on the plan of action, we began
        the arrangements required to select and recruit participants.
      </p>

      <dl class="rwc-aside">
        <div>
          <dt>My responsibilities</dt>
          <dd>Lead designer, co-researcher</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>The team</dt>
          <dd>1 lead designer (myself), 1 lead researcher</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Duration</dt>
          <dd>3 months</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <aside class="rwc-role-right">
      <div class="rwc-initiatives-title">Key initiatives</div>
      <ul class="rwc-initiatives-list">
        <li>Defined study goals and scope</li>
        <li>Screened and recruited participants</li>
        <li>Interviewed users</li>
        <li>Tested concept prototypes</li>
        <li>Processed insights</li>
        <li>Compiled insights into a Journey map</li>
        <li>Informed the company and product's roadmap</li>
      </ul>
    </aside>
  </section>

  {/* ───────────────────── THE CHALLENGE ───────────────────── */}
  <section class="rwc-section" id="case-challenge">
    <div class="rwc-challenge">
      <div class="rwc-challenge-text">
        <div class="eyebrow">The challenge</div>
        <h2 class="rwc-h2">Inform the future of our product</h2>
        <p>
          Roughly 1 year after we launched On-Air webinars, our product
          roadmap and core priorities were to deliver on the core needs of
          our users, catch up to our competitors' core benefits, and become a
          competitive force in the webinar space. But although our product
          was getting closer to what we had greater confidence on, we lacked
          a long-term vision on what it should become next, and a
          complementary way of informing our next priorities.
        </p>
        <p>
          At the time, we were defining our roadmap by scoring initiatives
          based on insights from sales calls, customer support requests,
          company townhall asks, and competitive benchmarks.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rwc-challenge-img">
        <div class="case-img-ph is-filled" data-ratio="4-3">
          <img src="/assets/images/cases/sy-research/registration.webp" alt="On-Air webinar registration page, April 2024" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
        <p class="case-img-caption">On-Air webinar registration page, April 2024.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ───────────────────── DEEP-DIVE ───────────────────── */}
  <section class="rwc-section" id="case-deep-dive">
    <h2 class="rwc-h2">Deep-dive with webinar organizers</h2>
    <p class="rwc-lead">
      Our goal was to recruit and interview non-StreamYard users who had
      significant experience with webinars, to understand their core needs,
      pain points, and capture their impressions from feature concept
      prototypes and the existing product experience.
    </p>

    {/* Screener + Interviews side by side */}
    <div class="rwc-options">
      <div class="rwc-option">
        <div class="case-img-ph is-filled" data-ratio="16-10">
          <img src="/assets/images/cases/sy-research/screener.webp" alt="User Interviews screener survey v2" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
        <h3>Searched for study candidates</h3>
        <p>
          Before the study, we decided to target highly experienced webinar
          organizers, who were paying for a similar product to achieve their
          goals, and that would potentially be StreamYard users. We did this
          by setting up a screener survey in the User Interviews platform,
          from which we found 11 potential fitting participants.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rwc-option">
        <div class="case-img-ph is-filled" data-ratio="16-10">
          <img src="/assets/images/cases/sy-research/interview.webp" alt="Zoom interview screenshot with participant" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
        <h3>Interviews and user-scenarios</h3>
        <p>
          We ran a series of interviews with participants ranging from
          healthcare, education, and corporate-comms industries. After each
          interview, we allocated 20 minutes for testing a user scenario,
          which involved presenting stimuli related to a potential new
          feature, running task scenarios, and gathering feedback.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* From notes to insights */}
    <div class="rwc-subsection">
      <div class="case-img-ph is-filled" data-ratio="16-9">
        <img src="/assets/images/cases/sy-research/insights-board.webp" alt="Dovetail-tagged interview notes aggregated into insight clusters" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <h3 class="rwc-h3">From notes to insights</h3>
      <p>
        Once all interviews were transcribed using Dovetail, relevant points
        were labeled accordingly, and notes began to be aggregated into
        insight areas. Some of the collected insight areas were product fit,
        engagement needs, post-webinar needs, and competitor impressions.
      </p>
    </div>

    {/* From insights into a journey map */}
    <div class="rwc-subsection">
      <div class="case-img-ph is-filled" data-ratio="16-9">
        <img src="/assets/images/cases/sy-research/journey-map.webp" alt="Webinar organizers' journey map — Plan / Prepare / Run / Debrief / Repurpose and Share" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <h3 class="rwc-h3">From insights into a journey map of the end-to-end experience</h3>
      <p>
        The webinar organisers' insights were then compiled into a journey
        map, which included 5 key areas that constitute the entire journey,
        from planning to repurposing and sharing. From here, our goal was to
        build this knowledge over time with insights collected, have the
        ability to drill down and understand specific steps of the journey
        in-depth, while creating specific journey maps per user segment.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ───────────────────── VALIDATION ───────────────────── */}
  <section class="rwc-section" id="case-validation">
    <div class="rwc-challenge">
      <div class="rwc-challenge-text">
        <h2 class="rwc-h2">
          We validated our assumptions, and informed our future roadmap.
        </h2>
        <p>
          The study's foundational insights and journey map were presented
          to the entire company, creating a scalable knowledge source and
          core insights to improve the product further, as well as providing
          insight into segment-specific needs.
        </p>
        <p>
          Particular insights were leveraged by the growth team to generate
          hypotheses, and led to new growth tests aimed at improving
          top-of-funnel growth.
        </p>
        <p>
          User scenarios played a crucial role as they helped us capture
          highly positive feedback on the concept of the feature. This
          positive reception gave us the confidence to proceed further
          with it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rwc-challenge-img">
        <div class="case-img-ph is-filled" data-ratio="4-3">
          <img src="/assets/images/cases/sy-research/slack-share.webp" alt="Slack post sharing the new webinar organizers' journey map with a Loom video overview" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ───────────────────── OUTCOMES & IMPACT ───────────────────── */}
  <section class="rwc-section" id="case-impact">
    <h2 class="rwc-h2">Outcomes and impact</h2>

    <div class="rwc-stats">
      <div class="rwc-stat">
        <div class="rwc-stat-n">1<span class="rwc-stat-unit">st</span></div>
        <div class="rwc-stat-desc">
          Knowledgebase of foundational webinar insights created in the
          company.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="rwc-stat">
        <div class="rwc-stat-n">2</div>
        <div class="rwc-stat-desc">
          Pods briefed with relevant cross-pod data (Growth and Library).
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="rwc-stat">
        <div class="rwc-stat-n">5</div>
        <div class="rwc-stat-desc">
          Insights used into ongoing product work.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</div>

<CaseBodyLightbox />

<style>
  /* UWO-specific overrides — shared .rwc-* layout/typography lives
     in global.css and the lightbox in CaseBodyLightbox.astro. */

  /* Slight tightening of subsection h3 spacing inside this body. */
  .rwc-subsection h3.rwc-h3 { margin-top: var(--dimension-space-24); }

  /* Challenge / Validation: 2-col text+image. */
  .rwc-challenge {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--dimension-space-48);
    align-items: start;
  }

  /* Option-compare tiles get a little more head-room than the
     global default (h3 starts at 20px, not 0). */
  .rwc-option h3 { margin-top: var(--dimension-space-20) !important; margin-bottom: var(--dimension-space-12) !important; }

  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .rwc-challenge { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
